course: dictionary
lesson: 3975
title: Gaelic: a language, a people, a sport
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gaelic can be a noun (a name for a group of languages) or an adjective (it describes something). The words next to it tell you which. In «In 1337, English rule in Ireland reached firmly only the area around Dublin, while Gaelic lords ruled most of the island», Gaelic is describing the lords, so it means belonging to the Gaels, the people who speak these languages.
explain: Now read «A rugby union team has 15 players on the pitch, and so does a Gaelic football team and a hurling team.» Here Gaelic is describing a football team. Ask: what word would fit here? The answer tells you it is an Irish sport, Gaelic football, which is often just called "Gaelic".
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: "a Gaelic football team" becomes "an Irish sport football team". It still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right. Check this with a dictionary if you are unsure.
fact: Gaelic is a group of Celtic languages. Irish (Gaeilge) is spoken in Ireland, and Scottish Gaelic is spoken in Scotland.
fact: Outside Ireland, Irish is often called Gaelic.
fact: Gaelic games are Irish sports: Gaelic football, hurling, camogie and handball.
fact: In Scotland, Gaelic is spoken in the Highlands and islands, and there are Gaelic-medium schools.
fact: The GAA stands for the Gaelic Athletic Association, which runs Gaelic games.
exercise: «In Ireland, children play Gaelic games at school.» What does Gaelic tell you about the games? | Scottish Gaelic only | They are played on ice | *They belong to the Irish sporting tradition of the Gaels | They are played with a ball made of glass
exercise: Gaelic is a group of languages. Which one is a Gaelic language? | Spanish | German | Italian | *Scottish Gaelic
exercise: According to «A rugby union team has 15 players on the pitch, and so does a Gaelic football team and a hurling team (rugby league has 13, Australian rules 18)», which sport has 13 players? | Hurling | *Rugby league | Rugby union | Gaelic football
test: In which part of Scotland is Gaelic spoken? | Only in Glasgow | In the Pale around Dublin | *In the Highlands and islands | Nowhere any more
test: What does GAA stand for? | Gaelic Art Academy | Global Adventure Academy | German Art Association | *Gaelic Athletic Association
exam: Which of these is NOT a Gaelic game? | Hurling | Camogie | Gaelic football | *Rugby union
